rtk-rewrite Hermes adapter
=========================

This repository contains a Hermes Agent plugin adapter for the RTK command
rewriter (https://github.com/rtk-ai/rtk).

The adapter code in ``__init__.py`` is derived from the RTK project's own
Hermes hook, ``hooks/hermes/rtk-rewrite/__init__.py``, which is distributed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Copyright and authorship of the
original hook belong to the RTK Contributors (see
https://github.com/rtk-ai/rtk/issues/3797 for provenance).

RTK itself is a separate project by the RTK Contributors, licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0. This adapter does not claim authorship of RTK or
of RTK's command-compression logic; all rewrite logic lives in the RTK binary.

This adapter is a thin bridge: it invokes the external ``rtk rewrite`` command
and returns the result to Hermes through the ``pre_tool_call`` modify
contract. It contains no rewrite logic of its own.

The rewritten command is returned to Hermes as an explicit ``modify``
directive instead of being assigned to the hook's ``args`` dict, and the
adapter adds a terminal-backend gate for Docker and remote targets. See
README.md.

This product includes software developed by the RTK Contributors.
